# Data conversion between kibibyte and petabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between kibibyte and petabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1KiB to 0.0000PB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5KiB yields 0.0000PB; backward, converting 1PB to 976562500000KiB preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5PB yields 1464843750000.0KiB. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1KiB
print(forward_whole->to(PB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5KiB
print(forward_fractional->to(PB))
backward_whole: int = 1PB
print(backward_whole->to(KiB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5PB
print(backward_fractional->to(KiB))

<<< stdout
0.0000PB
0.0000PB
976562500000KiB
1464843750000.0KiB

<<< stderr
